    "interpretation": [
      "classification_complete applies to the named finite required claims, not all possible behaviors of a format.",
      "Source-only questions are closed by reviewed source distinctions. No ordinary fixture or direct internal return is added as a new requirement.",
      "A selected ordinary clean control establishes only its stated baseline. A recognized limit or diagnostic is HOLD under the existing product normalization contract; validated malware evidence remains BLOCK.",
      "Conditional source claims retain their premises, including context retention, reporting reachability, suppressed-alert behavior and effective configuration. They are not universal ordinary-outcome promises.",
      "Historical pending fields and not-demonstrated lists remain unchanged in original artifacts. This supplement replaces the blanket finite-classification pending status, not the historical facts or unmeasured behaviors.",
      "The existing standard_engine_best_effort limitation permits explicit classified observability limits; unknown stopped obligations remain unresolved and are not automatically excluded."
    ],
